<title>UK: Christian Salvesen wins 20 mln stg contract.</title>
<headline>Christian Salvesen wins 20 mln stg contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Christian Salvesen Plc said on Wednesday its Swift Service industrial logistics division had won a three-year contract from automobile company Vauxhall, the British subsidiary of General Motors Corp, worth about 20 million stg.  </p>
<p>Swift will be responsible for distribution of all parts to Vauxhall's more than 450 dealers in the UK.</p>
<p>Swift has been responsible for deliveries into Vauxhall's production plant since 1992.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
